  "scope": "Complete the existing ordinary owning Package and shared-address Array path at 512 elements. Index and share immutable analysis facts while preserving complete source, initialization, loan ancestry and actual target checks. Analyze and independent Verify still derive and check their own results. Backend accounting follows the actual physical snapshot emission work without expanding the supported consumer profile.",
  "implementation": {
    "analyze": "Actual physical-slot and binding indexes, word-based liveness, complete immutable ancestry and instruction-local read candidates remove repeated lookup and temporary target work. Every retained-task, external and empty outer row is still charged and visited where required.",
    "verify": "Independent word liveness, current-arena ancestry, ordered paid loan unions, complete leaf-path indexes, physical source/result relation indexes, immutable per-instruction read candidates and immutable SSA loan-sequence groups. Invalid or missing loan IDs retain rejection order; unsupported groups use complete scans. Locals, retained ports, external facts and write access retain their original checks.",
    "backend": "Only Load and already materialized MakeAggregate/MakePackage snapshots use the actual machine-emission work calculation. Actual layout, complete metadata, source classification, allocation, clone, GEP, memcpy and typed loads/stores remain prepaid. Closure subtrees and other consumers retain the previous conservative path. Independent tests compare the complete old plan and machine module, not only hashes.",
    "unchanged_contracts": [
      "Default Limits and stack size",
      "Full original input bytes, element counts and functions",
      "Whole-array initialization from every actual source",
      "Borrow origins, permission modes and complete loan ancestry",
      "Managed ownership responsibility and cleanup",
      "Actual callee and physical machine ABI checks",
      "Independent raw and decoded Wire verification",
      "Public IR schema and dependencies"
    ]
  },
